	(text "I mean, this should be fine. The diode's forward voltage is about .32 V\nat the currents I am expecting. Therefore, if the G0 pulls to 0.1V LOW\nand the diode adds .32V, .42V must be less than .3Vdd for the NRST to \nregister VIL. If Vdd is 3.3V, this shouldn't be an issue I hope.  "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.038 113.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
